      "reactions": null,
      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "@{5e8bd6a1c129f205ff0684c8|full_name}: For me, the opposite is true. I leave most of my safety settings off and just auto-hide anything Very Poor. The problem is, though, some shaders like fur shaders can still be snuck in on good or medium avatars. It's a cute avatar, it's great, and you're a wonderful person, but I don't want to see it in an 80 person instance, and I don't want to hide everyone else with safety settings filtering you out, especially if you're trusted. But I also don't want to block your avatar and hurt your trust ranking, because I'd hate to be that person to knock you out of known or trusted. If I could just hide it in a specific instance, that'd be AMAZING.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    }
